  "evidence": [
    "Pinned get_group_volume4C5380 reads one dword at WaveControlGroup+4 with sixteen-entry unsigned index guard. Current source owns the real uint32_t group volume but copies it through memcpy into a local int. Pinned set_group_volume4C5320 reads the real inherited SoundFadeState volume_ dword immediately before virtual set_volume; the current source uses the same artificial scalar-copy pattern.",
    "Only the two selected implementation bodies may change: direct return of groups_[group].volume, and direct virtual wave->set_volume(wave->volume_). The now-unused local cstring include may be removed after checking all uses. No header, member type, signedness, symbol, annotation, guard, iteration or callback-order change. All52owner subjects are observation/preservation scope, not permission to rewrite their bodies.",
    "Keep uint32_t fields: Wave scaling depends on unsigned high-bit behavior. Conversion to signed int is implementation-defined for high-bit values, not permission to narrow the input domain. Require the pinned VC6 dword-bit behavior for all bit patterns through fresh identical physical emitted-code proof, and existing g++/clang actual-source tests including 0xC0000000 returned bits and 0x80000003 virtual arguments. Never clamp, normalize or insert a cast solely for codegen.",
    "Update the existing actual-source call assertion and damage mutant to the direct member-read spelling without dropping live-cursor, derived-virtual dispatch, enabled/poststore, error guards or high-bit cases. Include a wrong-field-read damage case proving the new source dependency is observed. Cheap actual-source tests precede compiler work.",
    "Require unchanged-replica and changed-body controls, existing two-profile owner match continuity, strict original/reference checks for the two targets, fresh actual application object correspondence/build/link and independent source review. Preserve all original identities, prior claims and seed discoveries; do not demote or reset task baselines. Reports remain ignored. Any unsupported preservation remains explicit, not an automatic/game acceptance claim."
  ],
  "intent": "Replace artificial scalar memory copies with genuine typed Wave_Device volume-field reads while preserving original dword bits, virtual-call timing, list mutation behavior and all historical obligations.",
